   <main class="wrap">
     <p class="eyebrow">Lewos</p><h1>Privacy</h1>
     <p class="intro">Lewos collects personal data only when you send it to us yourself.</p>
-    <section><h2>What we collect</h2><p>When you join First Access or book, we collect your name, email address, chosen weekend, group size, payment and booking status, the confirmations made during booking and anything you choose to tell us. Stripe handles your card details; Lewos does not receive or store the complete card number. When you use the question form, we collect your name, email address and question. To protect the forms from automated misuse, we temporarily process a one-way technical identifier derived from your network address and email address. It cannot be used by us to recover either value.</p><p>If you attend a filmed Tavern weekend, we may also process your filming preference and, where you consent, recordings containing your identifiable image or voice. The purpose and choices are explained separately before booking and filming.</p></section>
+    <section><h2>What we collect</h2><p>When you join First Access or book, we collect your name, email address, chosen weekend, group size, any extra nights you ask for, payment and booking status, the confirmations made during booking and anything you choose to tell us. Stripe handles your card details; Lewos does not receive or store the complete card number. When you use the question form, we collect your name, email address and question. To protect the forms from automated misuse, we temporarily process a one-way technical identifier derived from your network address and email address. It cannot be used by us to recover either value.</p><p>If you attend a filmed Tavern weekend, we may also process your filming preference and, where you consent, recordings containing your identifiable image or voice. The purpose and choices are explained separately before booking and filming.</p></section>
     <section><h2>Why</h2><p>To manage First Access, reserve and administer your booking, take payment, arrange your stay, comply with our legal obligations, or answer a question you send us.</p></section>
-    <section><h2>Where it goes</h2><p>Questions sent through the contact form are delivered through Netlify, the company that hosts this website. First Access requests, seat allocations and booking records are processed and stored using Supabase. Payments are handled by Stripe; Lewos does not receive or store your full card details. Transactional email may be delivered through Resend. These providers process the information only to provide those services to Lewos. We do not sell your details, share them with advertisers or add you to a list you did not request.</p></section>
+    <section><h2>Where it goes</h2><p>Questions sent through the contact form are delivered to Lewos by email through Resend. Netlify hosts this website and runs the code that handles the form. First Access requests, seat allocations and booking records are processed and stored using Supabase. Payments are handled by Stripe; Lewos does not receive or store your full card details. Transactional email may be delivered through Resend. These providers process the information only to provide those services to Lewos. We do not sell your details, share them with advertisers or add you to a list you did not request.</p><p>To arrange your stay we share part of your booking with the accommodation where the Tavern weekend takes place, Complejo Rural de Fontecha in Asturias, Spain. They receive your name, the size of your party, which weekend you booked, your arrival and departure dates, and any extra nights you asked for &mdash; what they need to prepare a room for you. They do not receive your email address, your allergies, your dietary requirements, or anything else you told us. Those stay with Lewos, and Lewos remains your contact for everything about your booking: general questions, dietary requirements, accessibility and anything unusual all go to <a href="mailto:lewos.co@gmail.com">lewos.co@gmail.com</a>. Fontecha is in Spain, so this part of your booking does not leave the European Economic Area.</p></section>
     <section id="transfers"><h2>Where in the world it goes</h2><p>Lewos works from Asturias in Spain, but the providers above are not all in Europe, so part of your information is processed outside the European Economic Area.</p><p>Netlify hosts this website and receives the contact form. Netlify, Inc. is established in the United States, transfers under the standard contractual clauses published by the European Commission, and is certified under the EU&ndash;U.S. Data Privacy Framework. Supabase stores the First Access and booking records and states that it may process them in the United States and Singapore, under those same standard contractual clauses. Payments run through Stripe's Irish entities, which use the standard contractual clauses and the EU&ndash;U.S. Data Privacy Framework for any onward transfer. Transactional email is delivered by Resend, which processes in the United States.</p><p>You can ask us for a copy of the safeguards that apply to any of these transfers. One email is enough.</p></section>
 
     <section><h2>How long we keep it</h2><p>Unsuccessful First Access requests and ordinary contact questions are kept only as long as needed to manage the request and reasonable follow-up. Confirmed booking, payment and invoice records are kept for the periods required by applicable accounting, tax and consumer law. A deletion request cannot override a legal duty to retain a particular record.</p><p>Filming preferences and consent records are kept for as long as needed to demonstrate and respect your choice. Recordings approved for use are kept while that use remains relevant, unless consent is withdrawn for future use. The technical identifier stops affecting access after its fifteen-minute protection window and is deleted automatically during subsequent security cleanup.</p></section>
